209 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 28 0 R /Fit ] /Next 210 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Title (S1. semantic.concept is a version-bound self-reference, so it carries no scientific meaning and breaks across versions)
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 28 0 R /Fit ] /Next 211 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 209 0 R /Title (S2. semantic.subject is uncontrolled free text compared by string equality)
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 29 0 R /Fit ] /Next 212 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 210 0 R /Title (S3. Direct compatibility hides required transformations: optional fields present on both contracts are never compared)
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 29 0 R /Fit ] /Next 213 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 211 0 R /Title (S4. unit-convertible is a four-row lookup table, not dimensional analysis, and no rule ties a unit to its quantity)
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 30 0 R /Fit ] /Next 214 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 212 0 R /Title (S5. biological_context.species is a single taxon compared by string equality, with no subsumption and an unsafe wildcard direction)
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 30 0 R /Fit ] /Next 215 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 213 0 R /Title (S6. Unit, scale and axis values in the generated fixtures are chosen by substring matching on the profile name)
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 31 0 R /Fit ] /Next 216 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 214 0 R /Title (S7. The single transformation fixture asserts a molar-concentration conversion for every measurement profile)
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 32 0 R /Fit ] /Next 217 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 215 0 R /Title (S8. The unit contradiction fixture asserts that g and kg are incompatible)
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 32 0 R /Fit ] /Next 218 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 216 0 R /Title (S9. No profile has a lossy or inference fixture, although the transformation policy declares both paths)
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 32 0 R /Fit ] /Next 219 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 217 0 R /Title (S10. UNKNOWN is only tested for a missing source; a missing target is never exercised)
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 33 0 R /Fit ] /Next 220 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 218 0 R /Title (S11. representation.kind uses exact equality, so lossless re-encodings are reported as contradictions)
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 33 0 R /Fit ] /Next 221 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 219 0 R /Title (S12. Identifier, consent and data-use fixtures carry placeholder values, and no namespace is constrained to a real registry)
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 34 0 R /Fit ] /Next 222 0 R /Parent 208 0 R /Prev 220 0 R /Title (S13. Uncertainty, detection limits and censoring are never required, though they change whether values are comparable)
>>
endobj
